#====================================================================
# DRAFT-mysqltuner-test-boundary-mysqladmin - upstream CLI tests can hide real mysqladmin dependencies
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-mysqltuner-test-boundary-mysqladmin
trigger_tool:           prove|mysqltuner|mysqladmin|mariadb-admin
phase:                  conan_build|test_triage
error_signature:        Couldn't find an executable mysqladmin/mariadb-admin command|Attempted to use login credentials, but they were invalid
severity:               2
category:               testing|external-client|perl|database
match_keywords:         mysqltuner, cli_validation.t, mysqladmin, mariadb-admin, no-service tests, authentication, TAP, database client
title:                  Do not classify upstream CLI validation as no-service when it shells out to mysqladmin
topic: >
  mysqltuner/2.9.1 tests/cli_validation.t mostly checks CLI parsing but its
  authentication test needs mysqladmin or mariadb-admin. On a worker without
  those commands, it fails before the expected invalid-credentials diagnostic.
root_cause: >
  File-level test names hid a command-level dependency. The authentication
  path cannot be validated without a MySQL/MariaDB client command.
durable_solution: >
  Exclude mysqladmin-dependent cases from build-time no-service TAP tests.
  Keep them deferred to a real database-client environment, or adapt/publish
  the database client as a separate dependency before making it part of CI.
rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           command-aware-test-triage
rec_command:            perl -S prove tests/cli_options.t tests/cli_forcemem_human.t tests/version_consistency.t tests/unit_version_helpers.t tests/unit_cli_helpers.t tests/unit_utilities.t
rec_auto_fix:           false
verification_cmd:       command -v mysqladmin || command -v mariadb-admin || echo defer-auth-validation
evidence_chain: >
  OHOS shadow CI ran cli_validation.t: 8 assertions passed, authentication
  assertion failed because mysqladmin/mariadb-admin was missing. Removing it
  from the no-service subset produced 6 files, 65 tests, PASS.
limitations: >
  This does not claim authentication behavior is validated. It records that
  validation belongs to a separate database-client test stage.
doc_file:               archives/m/mysqltuner/2.9.1/knowledge_drafts/DRAFT-mysqltuner-test-boundary-mysqladmin.md
last_updated:           2026-09-11
source_event:           mysqltuner 2.9.1 upstream TAP triage on OHOS shadow CI
metrics_success_count:  1
metrics_fail_count:     0
metrics_confidence:     0.9
draft:                  true
